		bodyHtml: `<p>Before the promise comes the reason for it. &ldquo;Have you not known? Have you not heard? Our Father is the everlasting Father, the Creator of the ends of the earth.&rdquo; (Isaiah 40:28). The renewal does not rest on the exiles. It rests on who he is.</p><p>The next words contrast him with them: &ldquo;He does not faint or grow weary; no one can fathom his understanding.&rdquo; (Isaiah 40:28). The people are tired; he is not. And verse 29 says what he does with that gap: &ldquo;He gives power to the weary, and increases strength for the powerless.&rdquo; (Isaiah 40:29).</p>`,
