		bodyHtml: `<p>Verse 30 is honest about human limits: &ldquo;Even youths will grow faint and weary, and young men will fall exhausted;&rdquo; (Isaiah 40:30). Even the strongest and youngest run out. The passage does not blame weariness on a lack of faith. It says weariness is what people are like.</p><p>That makes the "but" of verse 31 the turning point. Strength does not come from being the kind of person who never tires. It comes from where you turn when you do.</p>`,
